Filters manipulate data in Jinja2 (including the `template` module); several can live in one file (core ones are in `core.py`). They don't use the config system but can be documented since 2.14.
```python
try:
    cause_an_exception(with_undefined_variable)
except jinja2.exceptions.UndefinedError as e:
    raise AnsibleUndefinedVariable("... %s" % to_native(e))
except Exception as e:
    raise AnsibleFilterError("... %s" % to_native(e))
```
